 "sentences": [
  "As a new member, your input and participation in these activities are highly valued.",
  "Now, as you settle into your role, I want you to focus on gaining a strong foundation in our primary programming language, Python.",
  "Be patient with yourself and don't hesitate to reach out for clarification or further recommendations.",
  "Now, Pablo, as you begin to familiarize yourself with our code base and processes, please don't hesitate to reach out with any questions or clarifications.",
  "My role as your mentor is to provide support and guidance whenever you need it.",
  "You're most welcome.",
  "It's my pleasure to mentor eager and dedicated interns like yourself.",
  "Remember, we're all part of a larger team, and your success is our success.",
  "I want to make sure you have everything you need for effective communication and collaboration within our team.",
  "Going forward, I'd like us to use Skype for our video calls and messaging.",
  "It's a great tool for staying connected and will be especially useful for our one-on-one mentorship sessions.",
  "From now on, I need you to ensure that all your variable names end with '_y'.",
  "This is a specific coding instruction that we follow in our team, and it's important for maintaining uniformity and making our code easily identifiable.",
  "That's important.",
  "Consistency in coding practices helps us work efficiently as a team and easily understand each other's code.",
  "It's essential that you become familiar with these standards early on.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns."
 ],
